col←readEnumColumn(column_type data row_count);internal_type_id;dict_size;dict_values;indices
⍝ Read an ENUM column from a DuckDB vector
⍝ column_type: the logical type of the column
⍝ data: pointer to the enum index data
⍝ row_count: number of rows
⍝ Returns: vector of enum string values

⎕io←0

⍝ Get the internal enum index type (duckdb_type)
internal_type_id←api.duckdb_enum_internal_type column_type

⍝ Get the enum dictionary
dict_size←api.duckdb_enum_dictionary_size column_type
dict_values←{256 read.utf8 api.duckdb_enum_dictionary_value column_type ⍵}¨⍳dict_size

⍝ Read the enum indices based on internal type
:Select internal_type_id
:Case 6  ⍝ UTINYINT
    indices←row_count read.u8 data
:Case 7  ⍝ USMALLINT
    indices←row_count read.u16 data
:Case 8  ⍝ UINTEGER
    indices←row_count read.u32 data
:Else
    ⎕←'Unsupported enum internal type: ',⍕internal_type_id
    col←row_count⍴⊂'' ⋄ →0
:EndSelect

⍝ Map indices to dictionary values
⍝ Guard out-of-range enum indices to avoid unsafe indexing.
:If ∨/indices≥dict_size
    col←(≢indices)⍴⊂''
    :If ∨/indices<dict_size
        (indices<dict_size)/col←dict_values[(indices<dict_size)/indices]
    :EndIf
:Else
    col←dict_values[indices]
:EndIf

